{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_45edd50f2672648a1d4dfb2fc6024f86274fc6a17445bfb8ac58981e37078e60"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository includes run.py as CLI entry point, agents/recode/ implementation, envs/ wrappers for alfworld, webshop, and sciworld, configs/, and utils/ with an async OpenAI wrapper and constrained executor."},{"claim_ids":["clm_61c35d4d263c6703773a944e12e1bfef2e34c95b2b9742990c524edf78045add"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"LLM access is configured via named profiles in configs/profiles.yaml selected with --profile; OPENAI_API_KEY serves as a fallback, and cost tracking loads configs/prices.json with a track_costs toggle."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6eb3a3e434db03eeabec6b8c5c00994b0db0f6aff15dfba227c6dcfb732d7fab"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A constrained Python executor maintains environment variables, validates code blocks, and exposes the toolset available to the agent."},{"claim_ids":["clm_721246fc7c765c90322b6284177c63b2a4c18e25f74fac9250694bcd33ff0be1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Partial programs are organized in a tree where each node captures one sub-task and records its execution trace."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8a4871abab48bb47d8e6eef15a12b040b4a60235b39a18d3e11020d3bbbd1e26"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A dynamic execution loop executes each node immediately, with fresh observations deciding whether to expand further, retry, or finish."},{"claim_ids":["clm_95f55e37f0dd17298292ebc74421fff2e842e03f2211020afa3819da795845c3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"run.py exposes flags including -a/--agent, -e/--env, -n/--instances, -c/--concurrent, --split, --seed, --max-depth, --profile, and -C/--config for YAML-based flag overrides."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a4dfa0ef344f5a11532515bc193774a19b966baff05da8ed4b02e9fd649c3815"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README reports SFT experiments with Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct giving ReCode+SFT an average of 70.4% versus ReAct+SFT (67.6%) and CodeAct+SFT (55.8%)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cea2a64673e1fcee30bcf2a6881f8ec1146ed91798d6bdd0f32c7065e49b6cf9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"New environments implement a base Env contract with reset, _run, is_done, is_success, and report, plus per-environment prompts and few-shot files under agents/recode/resources/."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cf097eab89e8611c16a8261a2d5050cca27b04c5c56e6dc7c8fcff65c64064f9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: setup requires a conda environment with Python 3.10 or newer, and the README suggests configuring the three benchmark environments separately since dependency conflicts are unconfirmed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e098cece56a6f7c93277cc51090f0bfce3590d6f5e39ca1379775d691fc2e29a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README reports inference comparisons against ReAct, CodeAct, AdaPlanner, and ADaPT, claiming an average score of 60.8 (10.5 above the best baseline) and a perfect 100 in ALFWorld with claude-4-sonnet."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ffb847cc2ddf28386453d5bb775269e8eb5e5b60b2723a82e445d3b6bb8727c7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ReCode unifies plan and action into a single code representation, treating high-level plans as placeholder functions that recursively decompose into executable primitives."}],"claim_ids":["clm_45edd50f2672648a1d4dfb2fc6024f86274fc6a17445bfb8ac58981e37078e60","clm_61c35d4d263c6703773a944e12e1bfef2e34c95b2b9742990c524edf78045add","clm_6eb3a3e434db03eeabec6b8c5c00994b0db0f6aff15dfba227c6dcfb732d7fab","clm_721246fc7c765c90322b6284177c63b2a4c18e25f74fac9250694bcd33ff0be1","clm_8a4871abab48bb47d8e6eef15a12b040b4a60235b39a18d3e11020d3bbbd1e26","clm_95f55e37f0dd17298292ebc74421fff2e842e03f2211020afa3819da795845c3","clm_a4dfa0ef344f5a11532515bc193774a19b966baff05da8ed4b02e9fd649c3815","clm_cea2a64673e1fcee30bcf2a6881f8ec1146ed91798d6bdd0f32c7065e49b6cf9","clm_cf097eab89e8611c16a8261a2d5050cca27b04c5c56e6dc7c8fcff65c64064f9","clm_e098cece56a6f7c93277cc51090f0bfce3590d6f5e39ca1379775d691fc2e29a","clm_ffb847cc2ddf2838